        solution: 'Between same-direction currents the fields oppose. Zero where 6.0/x = 12/(0.30 − x) → x = 0.30 × 6/(6 + 12) = 0.10 m from the 6.0 A wire. F/L = 2 × 10⁻⁷ × 6.0 × 12/0.30 = 4.8 × 10⁻⁵ N/m, attractive.',
        calc: ['0.30 * 6.0 / (6.0 + 12)', 'P.C.mu0 * 6.0 * 12 / (2 * Math.PI * 0.30)'], answers: [0.1, 4.8e-5],
